{
  "id": "positivity-effect",
  "term": "positivity effect",
  "definition": "Positivity effect is the age-related tendency for cognitive processing to give relatively greater weight to positive than negative information. Compared with younger adults, older adults are more likely to pay attention to and remember positive material over negative material.",
